// Deal or Force - the ruins a war leaves (WarDamage.cs).
//
// Every region has a war damage from 0 (untouched) to 1 (ruins). Every day of battle in one of
// its provinces adds WarDamagePerBattleDay x the day's intensity, shared over the region's
// provinces, and the closer the region already is to ruins the less a day adds - so a region
// fought over for a year is mostly ruins and never more than that. The day's intensity is its
// casualties, both sides, over WarDamageBattleLosses, held between a quarter and three.
//
// Every economy week a damaged region
//   - makes less: its output is multiplied by 1 - WarDamageOutputLoss x the damage;
//   - lives worse: its standard of living falls by WarDamageLivingPerWeek x the damage;
//   - empties: WarDamageFleePerWeek x the damage of its people leave, WarDamageRefugeesStayHome
//     of them for the regions of their own country that are damaged less than
//     WarDamageSafeBelow (by how many people live there already) and the rest for the regions
//     of the neighbours at no war (the same way; with none, they are lost to the map). Those
//     who stayed in the country come home, WarDamageReturnPerWeek of them a week, once the
//     region is damaged less than WarDamageSafeBelow and has seen no battle for WarDamageSafeDays;
//   - and is rebuilt: the damage falls by WarDamageRecoveryPerWeek of itself, times one plus
//     WarDamageRecoveryPerInfrastructure for every level of infrastructure, times one plus the
//     country's reconstruction_speed modifier - and by a last thousandth, so it ends.
//
// A country can pay to rebuild one region (the region card's Rebuild, and the AI for its worst
// ruin): WarDamageRebuildCost x the damage x the region's share of the country's people x GDP.
// For WarDamageRebuildDays it is then rebuilt 1 + WarDamageRebuildBoost times as fast - as far
// as the market has the industrial materials it wants, and not while there has been a battle
// in the region in the last WarDamageSafeDays. Nothing under WarDamageRebuildMinimum is worth it.
// A country nobody plays orders it for a region at least WarDamageAiRebuildAbove in ruins when
// the treasury holds WarDamageAiRebuildReserve times the cost.
//
// Events and decisions can set the damage with "state.war_damage", and triggers can ask about
// the worst-hit region with "min_worst_war_damage" / "max_worst_war_damage".
//
// Every file in this folder is read in name order and later files win.
{
  "WarDamagePerBattleDay": 0.03,
  "WarDamageBattleLosses": 1500,
  "WarDamageRecoveryPerWeek": 0.012,
  "WarDamageRecoveryPerInfrastructure": 0.25,
  "WarDamageOutputLoss": 0.5,
  "WarDamageLivingPerWeek": 0.003,
  "WarDamageFleePerWeek": 0.004,
  "WarDamageRefugeesStayHome": 0.75,
  "WarDamageSafeBelow": 0.10,
  "WarDamageReturnPerWeek": 0.04,

  "WarDamageRebuildDays": 180,
  "WarDamageRebuildBoost": 2,
  "WarDamageRebuildCost": 0.25,
  "WarDamageSafeDays": 14,
  "WarDamageRebuildMinimum": 0.05,
  "WarDamageAiRebuildAbove": 0.20,
  "WarDamageAiRebuildReserve": 4
}
